inīna","verse_key":"2:236"},{"pos":26,"ar":"٢٣٦","en_gloss":"(236)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"2:236"}]},{"verse_key":"2:237","surah":2,"ayah":237,"ar_uthmani":"وَإِن طَلَّقْتُمُوهُنَّ مِن قَبْلِ أَن تَمَسُّوهُنَّ وَقَدْ فَرَضْتُمْ لَهُنَّ فَرِيضَةً فَنِصْفُ مَا فَرَضْتُمْ إِلَّآ أَن يَعْفُونَ أَوْ يَعْفُوَا۟ ٱلَّذِى بِيَدِهِۦ عُقْدَةُ ٱلنِّكَاحِ ۚ وَأَن تَعْفُوٓا۟ أَقْرَبُ لِلتَّقْوَىٰ ۚ وَلَا تَنسَوُا۟ ٱلْفَضْلَ بَيْنَكُمْ ۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ بَصِيرٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"If you divorce wives before consummating the marriage but after fixing a bride-gift for them, then give them half of what you had previously fixed, unless they waive [their right], or unless the one who holds the marriage tie waives [his right]. Waiving [your right] is nearer to godliness, so do not forget to be generous towards one another: God sees what you do.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَإِن","en_gloss":"And if","transliteration":"wa-in","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":2,"ar":"طَلَّقْتُمُوهُنَّ","en_gloss":"you divorce them","transliteration":"ṭallaqtumūhunna","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مِن","en_gloss":"from","transliteration":"min","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":4,"ar":"قَبْلِ","en_gloss":"before","transliteration":"qabli","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":5,"ar":"أَن","en_gloss":"[that]","transliteration":"an","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":6,"ar":"تَمَسُّوهُنَّ","en_gloss":"you (have) touched them","transliteration":"tamassūhunna","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَقَدْ","en_gloss":"while already","transliteration":"waqad","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":8,"ar":"فَرَضْتُمْ","en_gloss":"you have specified","transliteration":"faraḍtum","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":9,"ar":"لَهُنَّ","en_gloss":"for them","transliteration":"lahunna","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":10,"ar":"فَرِيضَةًۭ","en_gloss":"an obligation (dower)","transliteration":"farīḍatan","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos":11,"ar":"فَنِصْفُ","en_gloss":"then (give) half","transliteration":"faniṣ'fu","verse_key":"2:237"},{"pos"